  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Migrants, Displaced Persons and Local Communities in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With support from the Republic of Korea, this project contributes to enhancing the capacity of the Government of Kenya, migrants, displaced persons and local communities in Kenya to recover from crises including natural hazards and health emergencies. The International Organization for Migration aims to reach the most vulnerable by providing evidence-based humanitarian assistance in multi-purpose cash and settlement support as well as strengthening state capacity to prepare for, respond to and sustainably recover from health emergencies and natural and conflict-induced hazards.</narrative>
  </description>
